From a1ce030934a226a1a9ce72c461909715c5628c84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:08:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: optional waist yaw compensation of the pelvis turn
 (env.config.waist_yaw_comp reads the pelvis yaw change since the episode
 start at every step before the 0104 disturbance, one step behind like the
 real IMU, and adds minus gain times it, clamped to max_deg, to the waist yaw
 target that HOMIE sent, so that the torso carrying the arms keeps its
 heading; door_obs=torso turns the door frame position and orientation given
 to the policy back by the compensation, since the pelvis frame sees the door
 turn and the policy would also correct with the arm; hide_obs subtracts the
 compensation from the waist yaw angle and rate in the policy and HOMIE
 observations before the mirroring; on 11-11 the real stock legs turned the
 body by +10 to +29 deg just before the hand came down and the real runner can
 add to the waist target held through arm_sdk; with the disturbance imposed
 from outside, the reaction of the waist that would turn the real pelvis
 further is not modelled; default off = unchanged) (11-11)

